think HUNK58 landed the following window and named HUNK59 (windowed-finger classification) as the next crux. Took it.
think The design fork: continuous auto-pan risks finger creep at a held pixel (classify against a moving window → seek → window pans → same pixel maps higher). Chose the provable form — a GESTURE WINDOW snapshotted at the press and frozen through the drag, so the band under the finger equals the marked band with no creep and no drift. Continuous auto-pan is named for a later rung.
think FilmstripTrackScrub owns one FilmstripTrack + scrubbing flag + gesture_first. finger_down captures window_first() as gesture_first; move/up classify x against the frozen window (scrub_step → gesture_first + clamped band); paint shows the frozen window while armed and the following window when idle, so the display matches the finger during the drag and re-centers on lift.
think The crux value: HUNK56's whole-strip scrub calls filmstrip (whole), which refuses FilmstripTooWide for a 64-edit history — so long histories could not be scrubbed at all. The windowed scrub paints and scrubs them. The selftest proves the whole strip refuses, then scrubs the same history band by band.
obs Built and GREEN first metal run — no RED this lap. Two-plus asserts per fn, all invariants positive; TAME bans clean, width exit 0. No existing file touched, so no regression.
obs Selftest also proves: a second press re-centers a fresh gesture window; a scrub pins at both shown ends (unlike a tap); a scrub forgets nothing (redo tail survives a back-scrub); an unarmed move fires nothing; a scrubbed window rasterizes lit.
